RM(1)                          User Commands                           RM(1)

NAME
    rm - remove a file or an empty directory

SYNOPSIS
    rm NAME

DESCRIPTION
    Remove the entry NAME from the working directory. A file's data is
    freed when its last name goes (see ln(1) and the link count in
    stat(1)). A directory must be empty; one that is not is refused.

    NAME is one name in the working directory, not a path. Removing it
    needs the right to delete entries in that directory.

    The system trees (/bin, /sbin, /lib, /usr) refuse every change, by
    every login including the administrator's: they are rebuilt at each
    boot from the kernel-verified boot modules (hier(7)).

SEE ALSO
    mkdir(1), ln(1), stat(1)
